    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0287" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg191"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Sherman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2917.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that
                    Kwangchau Bay, which has been recently ceded to the French Government for
                    ninety-nine years, is situate on the southwestern coast of China, in the
                    district of Leichou, Kwangtung Province.</p>
                <p>The harbor is said to be a good one. The country back of it is highly productive.
                    One of the chief products is sugar.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
